I. Intent of the Clanker Repository
- Showcase an efficient, terminal-driven utility for local LLM prompt assembly and context injection.
- Serve as a modular tool designed to inspect, refactor, and evolve codebases (including itself).

II. Intended Audience
- Developers and "vibe coders" looking to streamline context injection into browser-based LLMs.
- Technical recruiters and engineers evaluating software design, architecture, and Python competency.

III. Intended Impression (Emergent from content)
- Pragmatic and developer-focused: Solves real context-assembly overhead in terminal workflows.
- Modular & extensible: Clean separation of concerns (engine, services, adapters, models).
- Meta-aware: Self-refining architecture designed to operate on its own source files.

IV. Structure
1. Title & Value Proposition (Quick pitch on browser-based vibe-coding elevation)
2. Core Features & Key Concepts (YAML configurations, context resolvers, keyboard navigation)
3. Installation & Quickstart (Cloning, making executable, terminal usage)
4. Context & Architecture Overview (Brief breakdown of how resolvers, templates, and domain layouts fit together)
5. Project Status & Roadmap

V. Style
- Direct, functional, and developer-friendly.
- Concise with minimal fluff; heavy use of code snippets and ASCII terminal hints where applicable.

VI. Call to Action
- Clone or copy `clanker.py` to get started locally.
- Use Clanker on itself to explore custom YAML configurations and prompt assembly.